# ED - Edit text with the line editor

```text
ED filespec [output-DU:]
```

## Create a file

For a new file, start ED D0:NOTE.TXT and type I followed by Enter. Type
your text, then press Ctrl-Z to return to command mode. B moves to the
beginning of the buffer and #T types the remaining lines.

## Edit and save

For an existing file, #A reads as much source text as fits into the
buffer. Make your edits and enter E alone to finish and save. Q alone
abandons unpublished edits immediately. For a full-screen editor, see
[TED](TED.HLP).
